# The Training menu's speech in a Training match: Pichu against the CPU on
# a random stage. Start opens the menu with the keys, the cursor walks every
# row down to Finish and on round to Speed, Speed goes through its six
# words, each value row changes once each way, Up goes round to CP Damage,
# skipping the hidden row, and a held Right there says its first value, the
# game's first repeat and the value it settles on. Start closes the menu
# on CP Damage and opens it again without the keys, and Finish leaves for
# Training character select.
# Run with the default --scene title:
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py tools/a11y/training_menu.drive
# drive.py turns steering on (MELEE_A11Y_STEER=1). The menu takes the main
# stick and the D-pad alike; the steps use the stick, as a held D-pad would
# not differ.
# A line that should be absent cannot fail a script: run_level.py fails a
# run that names the hidden row or speaks a number more often than the
# steps below do (the held Right's repeats between its first two lines and
# the settled one).

# Title screen to the main menu (tools/a11y/main_menu.drive).
wait "state 0 scene 0$"
press Start until "boot scene: game mode"
press A until "boot scene: state 0 scene 1$" 20 0.3
wait '"Main Menu\. 1-P Mode\. '
sleep 1

# 1-P Mode, Training.
press A
wait '"1-P Mode\. Regular Match\. '
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait '"Event Match\. '
press Down
wait '"Stadium\. '
press Down
wait '"Training\. '
sleep 0.3
press A
wait '"Training character select\. Player 1, no character\. CPU, (?P<cpu>.+)\."$'
sleep 1

# Pichu, which makes the match ready (tools/a11y/css_training.drive), and
# Start on stage select for a random stage.
press DUp
wait ': "Pichu(, the CPU.s coin)?"$'
wait 'glide to "Pichu[^"]*" ended after \d+ frames: arrived'
press A
wait 'Ready to fight\. Press Start\.'
sleep 0.5
press Start
wait '"Stage select\. '
sleep 1
press Start
wait 'boot scene: state \d+ scene 4$'

# Start opens the menu once the match lets it pause; the first opening of a
# session has the keys. The menu speaks nothing more until a press changes
# what it shows, so the waits below each name the press's own line, and
# the sleeps keep each press past the 0.15 s settle after the line before,
# where it is said at once.
press Start until '"Training menu\. Speed: x1\. Up and down for rows, left and right to adjust, A on Item, Reset and Finish, Start to close\."$' 20 1
sleep 1

# Speed's six words, Right going slower and wrapping from 1/4 to x2.
press Right
wait ': "2/3"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "1/2"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "1/4"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "x2"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "x1\.5"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "x1"$'
sleep 0.3

# Every row down, each value once each way.
press Down
wait ': "Item: Food"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "Maxim Tomato"$'
sleep 0.3
press Left
wait ': "Food"$'
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait ': "No\. of CPs, 1"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "2"$'
sleep 0.3
press Left
wait ': "1"$'
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait ': "CP, Stand"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "Walk"$'
sleep 0.3
press Left
wait ': "Stand"$'
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait ': "CP Damage: 0"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "1"$'
sleep 0.3
press Left
wait ': "0"$'
sleep 0.3
# The hidden row between is skipped.
press Down
wait ': "Camera: Normal"$'
sleep 0.3
press Right
wait ': "Zoom"$'
sleep 0.3
press Left
wait ': "Normal"$'
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait ': "Reset"$'
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait ': "Finish"$'
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait ': "Speed: x1"$'
sleep 0.3

# Up round from Speed to CP Damage, skipping the hidden row the other way.
press Up
wait ': "Finish"$'
sleep 0.3
press Up
wait ': "Reset"$'
sleep 0.3
press Up
wait ': "Camera: Normal"$'
sleep 0.3
press Up
wait ': "CP Damage: 0"$'
sleep 0.3

# Right held two seconds. The press says "1" at once; the game's first
# repeat comes 20 ticks later, past the 0.15 s settle, so "2" is said too.
# The next two repeats come about 0.15 s apart, right on the settle, so either
# may be said; the quicker ones after them are held back, and the value
# they settle on is said 0.15 s after the last, once the stick is let go.
# How many repeats a hold gets depends on the input driver's timing, so the
# settled value is kept, not pinned.
press Right 2000
wait ': "1"$'
wait ': "2"$'
wait 'pad: btn 0000 stick 0,0 '
wait ': "(?P<damage>[1-9]\d+)"$'
sleep 0.5

# Start closes the menu, saying nothing; the next Start opens it on the row
# it was left on, without the keys.
press Start
sleep 1
press Start
wait '"Training menu\. CP Damage: %damage%\."$'
sleep 1

# Down to Finish, and A leaves Training for its character select.
press Down
wait ': "Camera: Normal"$'
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait ': "Reset"$'
sleep 0.3
press Down
wait ': "Finish"$'
sleep 0.3
press A
wait '"Training character select\. '
sleep 1
